      "index": 1,
      "simplified": "\n\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Ben’s Diary – My Cat Is Sick?"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "simplified": "今天，有个人对我说：“你有毛病啊？”",
      "traditional": "今天，有個人對我說：“你有毛病啊？”",
      "pinyin": "jīn tiān yǒu ge rén duì wǒ shuō nǐ yǒu máo bìng a",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "simplified": "\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Today, someone said to me: “What’s wrong with you?”"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "simplified": "我一听，“猫”？“病”？我回答他：“我的猫没有病。”",
      "traditional": "我一聽，“貓”？“病”？我回答他：“我的貓沒有病。”",
      "pinyin": "wǒ yì tīng māo bìng wǒ huí dá tā wǒ de māo méi yǒu bìng",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "simplified": "\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "I heard “cat” and “sick”? So I answered him: “My cat isn’t sick.”"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "simplified": "那个人很奇怪地看着我，说：",
      "traditional": "那個人很奇怪地看著我，說：",
      "pinyin": "nà ge rén hěn qí guài de kàn zhe wǒ shuō",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "simplified": "“还真的是有毛病！”说完就走了。",
      "traditional": "“還真的是有毛病！”說完就走了。",
      "pinyin": "hái zhēn de shì yǒu máo bìng shuō wán jiù zǒu le",
      "english": "That person looked at me very strangely and said:"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "simplified": "\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "“There really is something wrong with you!” finished talking and walked away."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "simplified": "后来，我才知道他说的是“有毛病”，不是“有猫病”。",
      "traditional": "後來，我才知道他說的是“有毛病”，不是“有貓病”。",
      "pinyin": "hòu lái wǒ cái zhī dào tā shuō de shì yǒu máo bìng bú shì yǒu māo bìng",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "simplified": "他是在骂我。",
      "traditional": "他是在罵我。",
      "pinyin": "tā shì zài mà wǒ",
      "english": "Only afterward did I realize that what he said was “have something wrong”, and not “the cat is sick”."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "simplified": "\n",
      "traditional": "\n",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "He was cursing at me."
    }
  ],
